<title>USA: Texaco reaches settlement in bias case - lawyer.</title>
<headline>Texaco reaches settlement in bias case - lawyer.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texaco Corp. settled a federal discrimination lawsuit filed by black employees, one of the lawyers for the plaintiffs said Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;We have settled the case. We think it is precedent setting,&quot; said Attorney Daniel Berger.  </p>
<p>Berger would not release further details of the settlement but said a news conference was scheduled for Friday afternoon.</p>
<p>&quot;All I can say is we are very ecstatic,&quot; said Berger.</p>
<p>The lawsuit, filed by black employees in 1994, charges the oil giant with systematically discriminating against blacks and denying them promotions.</p>
<p>Civil rights leader Jessie Jackson, who with a coalition of other black leaders called a national boycott on Tuesday against Texaco until the lawsuit is settled, is to attend the Washington news conference.</p>
</text>
